  "title_lines": [
   "TK 95 31",
   "CHIRAL LAGRANGIANS FOR BARYONS",
   "COUPLED TO MASSIVE SPIN\u20131 FIELDS \u22c6"
  ],
  "abstract": "We analyze the e\ufb00ective low\u2013energy \ufb01eld theory of Goldstone bosons and baryons chirally coupled to massive spin\u20131 \ufb01elds. We use the electromagnetic baryon form factors to demonstrate the formal equivalence between the vector and the tensor \ufb01eld formulation for the spin\u20131 \ufb01elds. We also discuss the origin of the so\u2013called Weinberg term in pion\u2013nucleon scattering and the role of \u03c1\u2013meson exchange. Chirally coupled vector mesons do not give rise to this two\u2013pion nucleon seagull interaction but rather to higher order corrections. Some problems of the formal equivalence arising in higher orders and related to loops are touched upon.",
  "docinfo": {
   "Title": "arXiv:hep-ph/9511320v1  15 Nov 1995",
